TASK-186.3 runtime harness: the dev toolbar's capture buttons (visible area
and full page; click copies, Option-click saves) on a single tab, in a split
(the unfocused pane's button) and with the docked Web Inspector open, at 2x.
Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task186-3-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # Retina on a 1x monitor: the TASK-110 virtual display (docs/task-110/vdisplay.m),
    #   clang -fobjc-arc -framework Foundation -framework CoreGraphics vdisplay.m -o vdisplay
    #   ./vdisplay &   (a 1600x1000 pt @2x screen until killed); the harness
    #   moves the window onto the first 2x screen.
    # $SITE/tall.html: 10 coloured 500 px bands, a fixed 40 px header, a sticky
    # 60 px bar, a 2D canvas (orange) and a 60 px magenta BOTTOM MARKER, 5320 px
    # tall; app.html / api.html: solid #2a7fff / #ffb000.
    python3 -m http.server 8863 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory "$SITE" &
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify1863 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT=8863 \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # a watcher captures `screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber>` for each
    # "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>" line of $OUT/verify.log; the harness waits
    # for each PNG. Wait for "done" (about 65 s), then kill that pid, the
    # server and vdisplay.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task186-3-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    rm -r -- ~/Library/Application\ Support/DetourVerify1863

Seams: the window's capturePasteboard is a private named pasteboard
(com.detourbrowser.verify.task1863) and captureSaveDirectory is $OUT/saved,
so the user's clipboard and ~/Downloads are untouched. Buttons are pressed
with performClick on the group's own buttons (through the window's wiring);
Option is simulated through the group's modifierFlags seam. Each PNG is read
back from the pasteboard and written to $OUT. The inspector is opened with
WebInspectorToggler (step 5); no __WebInspector default was added (before
and after: only WebKit2InspectorStartsAttached = 1).

Results (2026-10-24, macOS 26.7, window 1400x860 on the 2x virtual display,
backingScaleFactor 2; three runs, the last below; every PNG and window
capture read and matching the log):
